Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,A man lay in a sealed\Nroom for four days.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.02,0:00:05.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,He could not see,\Nhear, taste,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.45,0:00:07.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,smell, or feel\Nanything.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.70,0:00:10.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then he began to hear\Nhis dead wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.44,0:00:12.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,Why did the scientists\Nkeep listening?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.84,0:00:14.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,What did they want\Nfrom him?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.48,0:00:16.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,Let us go back to the\Nbeginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.70,0:00:19.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,In nineteen\Neighty-three, a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.07,0:00:22.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,group of deeply\Nreligious scientists
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.23,0:00:23.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,ran a secret test in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.99,0:00:26.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,an undisclosed\Nfacility.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.40,0:00:28.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,They believed the five\Nsenses
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.68,0:00:31.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,clouded our view of\Neternity.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.26,0:00:34.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,Take them away, they\Nthought, and a human
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.36,0:00:37.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,mind could reach God\Nby thought alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.68,0:00:40.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,They chose an elderly\Nman who said
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.33,0:00:43.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,he had nothing left to\Nlive for.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.12,0:00:44.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,He volunteered.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.52,0:00:47.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,Surgeons cut every\Nnerve that carried
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.66,0:00:50.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,feeling from his body\Nto his brain.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.92,0:00:53.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,His muscles still\Nworked, but
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.38,0:00:55.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,he could no longer\Nsee, hear,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.84,0:00:58.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,taste, smell, or feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.16,0:00:59.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,Nothing reached him\Nfrom
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.80,0:01:01.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,the outside world.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.33,0:01:04.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,The scientists watched\Nthrough the glass, and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.68,0:01:08.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,a tape recorder caught\Nhis slurred words.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.04,0:01:10.22,Cap,,0,0,0,,He could not hear\Nhimself speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.24,0:01:13.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,After four days, he\Nsaid hushed voices
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.29,0:01:16.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,were speaking inside\Nhis head.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.15,0:01:18.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,Two days later, he\Nsaid his dead
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.59,0:01:20.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,wife was talking to\Nhim, and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.72,0:01:22.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,that he could answer\Nher.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.92,0:01:25.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then he began naming\Ndead relatives
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.77,0:01:27.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,of the scientists.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.54,0:01:29.53,Cap,,0,0,0,,He repeated private\Ndetails
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.55,0:01:31.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,that only their\Nspouses and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.56,0:01:33.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,parents could have\Nknown.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.87,0:01:36.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,For a week, the voices\Nfilled
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.17,0:01:38.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,every waking moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.05,0:01:40.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,He threw his body\Nagainst the wall,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.75,0:01:43.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,hoping for pain to\Ndrown them out.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.67,0:01:45.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,He begged for\Nsedatives, so he
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.87,0:01:47.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,could escape by\Nsleeping.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.01,0:01:50.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,Sleep brought\Nnightmares, and in
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.45,0:01:53.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,them, the dead were\Nwaiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.03,0:01:55.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then the voices turned\Nhostile.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.29,0:01:58.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,They spoke of hell and\Nthe end of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.46,0:02:01.33,Cap,,0,0,0,,For five hours, he\Nshouted that there
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.35,0:02:04.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,was no heaven and no\Nforgiveness.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.23,0:02:06.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,The scientists were\Ncertain
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.12,0:02:07.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,he was close to God.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.98,0:02:09.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,Soon he could no\Nlonger
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.58,0:02:10.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,form a sentence.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.99,0:02:13.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,He lost control of his\Nbody, and
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.59,0:02:15.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,the team had to tie\Nhim down
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.86,0:02:18.65,Cap,,0,0,0,,so he could not harm\Nhimself.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.67,0:02:21.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,At last, though he was\Nblind, he turned
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.84,0:02:24.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,his head and looked\Nstraight at
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.36,0:02:27.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,a scientist for the\Nfirst time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.18,0:02:29.79,Cap,,0,0,0,,He whispered that he\Nhad spoken with
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.81,0:02:32.43,Cap,,0,0,0,,God, and God had\Nabandoned them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.45,0:02:34.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then his vital signs\Nstopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.86,0:02:37.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,No cause of death was\Never found.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.88,0:02:40.96,Cap,,0,0,0,,This video is inspired\Nby the story
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.98,0:02:43.88,Cap,,0,0,0,,Gateway of the Mind,\Nas published
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.90,0:02:47.07,Cap,,0,0,0,,on an online horror\Nstory page.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.09,0:02:48.73,Cap,,0,0,0,,Would you have kept\Nlistening
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.75,0:02:49.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,to the voices?
